  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a medium saucepan of water to the boil for the noodles. Meanwhile, thinly slice the onion. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Coarsely chop the broccoli stem into 1cm chunks, then cut the head into small florets.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144672/photos/large/prep_vegetables-6012e6adec9c649f0ce175e064d9e21a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook noodles: Cut the tofu into 1.5cm pieces. Combine the hoisin, 1 tbs soy sauce, 1½ tbs boiling water and 1 tsp honey in a bowl and season with pepper. Cook the noodles in the pan of boiling water for 8 mins or until tender. Drain.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144673/photos/large/prep_tofu_and_sauce-55490d69816adb2c2292f0c2560045fd.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir-fry tofu and veggies: Meanwhile, heat 1 tbs vegetable oil in a large frypan over high heat. Stir-fry the tofu for 2-3 mins until golden. Remove from the pan with a slotted spoon. Add the broccoli stems and stir-fry for 1 min. Add the onion, broccoli florets and garlic and stir-fry for 2 mins or until starting to brown.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144674/photos/large/stir_fry_tofu-03b237e9be16b011ed4d5d8538fab584.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add noodles: Reduce the heat to medium. Add the tofu and hoisin mixture to the vegetables and stir-fry for 1 min or until the vegetables are softened but still have crunch. Add the noodles and toss gently to combine. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144675/photos/large/add_sauce-af49f3ad4d15a75600e5b9ba2f1d2288.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the stir-fry among bowls. Scatter with the sesame seeds and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144676/photos/large/serve_up-495331be28046ea21e3316c3bed80aa9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know?: Glass noodles are also called sweet potato noodles, but they aren't the spiralized noodles made from sweet potatoes – these are slightly chewy, translucent noodles made using sweet potato starch.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144677/photos/large/make_it_yours-5f42fae2a3c6450b54a3156948e8a007.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
